\ ==== unread-local warning ====

\ A local that is assigned or received but never read draws a compile warning
\ naming the definition, with the file and line when the definition was loaded.
\ Reads of any kind count, a do index is exempt, and the warning never blocks
\ the definition.

\ -- assigned by to, never read
: leftover 3 to scratch 4 ;
leftover . cr

\ -- received in the head, never read
: ignores | a b | b ;
1 2 ignores . cr

\ -- a read anywhere counts, including inside a branch or a nested quotation
: read-in-branch 0 to seen 1 if seen then ;
: read-in-quotation 5 to base [: base :] execute ;
read-in-branch . read-in-quotation . cr

\ -- a do index that only counts repetitions is not reported
: repeat-three 0 3 1 do k "x" . loop cr ;
repeat-three

\ -- a loaded definition reports its file and line
": loaded-leftover | n | 10 to unused n ;" "/tmp/docs-unread.telic" write-file
"/tmp/docs-unread.telic" load
7 loaded-leftover . cr

\ -- a quotation's own unread local names the enclosing definition
: outer [: 1 to inner-scratch 2 :] execute ;
outer . cr
